§ `ss 3(3), (4) and 18(1)`

#ASSERT `section 3 applies to the ship` `a laden tanker`
#ASSERT `section 3 applies to the ship` `an empty tanker in ballast`
#ASSERT `section 3 applies to the ship` `a combination carrier with ore after oil`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 applies to the ship` `a combination carrier proved clean`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 applies to the ship` `a container ship`
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 applies to the ship` `a naval tanker`

§ `ss 3 and 4`

#ASSERT `the owner is liable under section 3` `a laden tanker` `the crew's negligent navigation`
#ASSERT NOT `the owner is liable under section 3` `a laden tanker` `an act of war`
#ASSERT `the owner is liable under section 3` `a laden tanker` `an ordinary storm`
#ASSERT `the owner is liable under section 3` `a laden tanker` `sabotage by the owner's own employee`
#ASSERT `the owner is liable under section 3` `a laden tanker` `sabotage by an outsider combined with crew negligence`

§ `s 5(1)(d), (2)`

#ASSERT `the person is shielded by section 5` `the master of the polluting ship` FALSE
#ASSERT `the person is shielded by section 5` `a bareboat charterer` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the person is shielded by section 5` `a salvor acting on its own initiative` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the person is shielded by section 5` `the owner of the oil cargo` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the person is shielded by section 5` `a clean-up contractor` TRUE

§ `s 5(3)`

#ASSERT `the loss is recoverable from the owner` `contamination damage to a hotel's beachfront`
#ASSERT `the loss is recoverable from the owner` `a fish farm's lost profits from the contaminated water`
#ASSERT NOT `the loss is recoverable from the owner` `the abstract value of the harm to the marine environment`

